tags: host-name, domain, dns

A kind of network: one host name and its ports. The instance can connect to the IPv4
addresses of the name, on these ports only.

The value is key=value lines, sorted by key, separated by a newline. The key host is
required: a lowercase DNS name with at least one ".". The key port is optional: a port
from 1 to 65535. With no port, the ports are 80 and 443. Another key is not valid.
Example: host=api.example.com and port=8443, one on each line.

The node finds the members at each start: it resolves the A records of the name with
its own resolver. It does not use IPv6. The node is bound.

=== formal
class=domain
ipv6=not used: the node does not use the addresses of 128 bits (the AAAA records)
members=the addresses of 32 bits (the document 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:5efb1730c69ebce4f33d2d940d1e3e03f2fe3910fc0a49739f8c478c7f550bb7) of the A records (section 3.4.1 of the document 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:f17c0393548b0632774637f18e10e7a92084f5403915b61ad03648fa14f2e25c) of host, which the node resolves at the start, on the ports
name=host-name
port.default=80 and 443
value=key=value lines sorted by key: host (required: a domain name of section 3.1 of the document 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:f0baa0620a4d5e430122c810a80d1884c7beca0146ae836e0ce9212282439bfe, with the letters in lowercase and at least one '.'), port (optional: a port of section 3.1 of the document 0e5751c026e543b2e8ab2eb06099daa1d1e5df47778f7787faab45cdf12fe3a8:f8a0a6609035df7f645e13152b1a325cfb13c31a7983d53a47b33dd827d8708c, 1 to 65535, base 10); no other key
